// PARAM: --analysis congruence
// a is concretely 6. The context-insensitive run cannot say so.
//
// The concrete mechanism is the shared callee context. Ctx_None gives
// twice one FunctionEntry slot for both call sites, so p is seeded with
// the join of the singletons 3 and 5. That join is the smallest residue
// class containing both, 3 (mod 2); p * 2 carries it to 2 (mod 4); and
// congruence_eqb declines on a non-singleton. Nothing is lost inside the
// callee -- the transfer is exact on the class it was given.
//
// ../precision/07-entry_state_separates_calls.vimp is the same program
// under --context entry-state, where the two seeds stay apart and both
// checks are decided.
fun twice(p) { return p * 2; }
fun main() {
  a = twice(3);
  b = twice(5);
  __voblint_check(a == 6); // UNKNOWN
}
